CC BY-NC 4.0 (see LICENSE). It is free for academic and other non-commercial use.
Uses beyond those permitted by the license must be discussed with the authors
of STAPLE.

Changes made to the original work
---------------------------------
* The MATLAB code used by STAPLE's hip_model workflow (STAPLE pelvis, GIBOC femur
  with cylinder fit, Kai2014 tibia, auto2020 joints, OpenSim model generation)
  was translated to Python (numpy, scipy and the OpenSim Python API).
* MATLAB toolbox functions were replaced by equivalents: Curve Fitting Toolbox
  fits (fitCSA) by scipy.optimize, convhull by scipy.spatial, reducepatch by the
  fast-simplification package.
* computeMassProperties_Mirtich1996 was replaced by TriInertiaPpties (the MATLAB
  function has an error in the products of inertia, which does not affect the
  final models).
* Paths of the visualization meshes in the .osim files use "/" as separator.
* Command line interface, tests against MATLAB outputs and comparison tools were
  added.
No other change of the algorithms is intended; results are verified against
MATLAB STAPLE (see README.md).

How to cite
-----------
If you use pystaple, please cite the STAPLE publication, as requested by its
authors:

    Modenese L., Renault J.-B. (2021). Automatic generation of personalised
    skeletal models of the lower limb from three-dimensional bone geometries.
    Journal of Biomechanics 116, 110186.
    https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jbiomech.2020.110186

and the publications of the algorithms you use (see README.md).

Data
----
The bone geometries and MATLAB outputs in reference/ are derived from the
bone_datasets distributed with STAPLE and are subject to their own terms, see
reference/DATA_LICENSES.md. They are not part of the Python package.
